titre $ Pyrenophora  Eriksson 
com$ Fr.Lit.: Eriksson O. 1967a: 373, Crivelli 1983: 115, Barr 1990: 10. adapt GF Juin 09
1,2 $ Sp. flattened 
1,3 $ Sp. rounded in section
2,0 $ Sp. flattened, with 3 travisepta, all segments with longisepta, hyaline, with mucous sheath; on Typha, phen.: V $ P. typhaecola (Cooke) E. Müll., Sydowia 5: 256 (1951)
2,0 $ Sp. flattened, 3-41x16-18x3-14 µm, with 3 travisepta, pale yellow-brown, with very thin mucous sheath; on Hierochloë alpina $ P. macrospora (J. Schröt.) Wehm., Pleospora Monograph: 278 (1961)
3,4 $ Sp. dark brown, thick-walled, with 5 or 5-7 or 7 travisepta, 25-45x10-16,5 µm; alpine
3,5 $ Sp. hyaline or pale colored or sp. larger
4,0 $ Ascomata 120-150 µm diam.; sp. with 5 travisepta, 26-34x10-13,5 µm; on Phleum $ P. phlei (E. Müll.) Crivelli, Diss. ETH Zürich 7318 : 122 (1983)
4,0 $ Ascomata 150-250 µm diam.; sp. with 5 travisepta, 28-37,5x11,5-16,5 µm; on Tresitumdistichophyllum, phen.: VII-IX . $ P. raetica (E. Müll.) Crivelli, Diss. ETH Zürich 7318: 121 (1983)
4,0 $ Ascomata 200-300 µm diam.; sp. with (5)7 travisepta, 32-43,5x12-16 µm; on Poa alpina ; phen.: VII-VIII $ P. subalpina (E. Müll.) Crivelli, Diss. ETH Zürich 7318: 120 (1983)
5,6 $ Sp. with 3 travisepta, end cells without longisepta
5,7 $ Sp. with 5 ore more travisepta
6,0 $ Sp. ellipsoid, 3-72x17-30x14-25 µm, with 3 travisepta and one longiseptum in one or both median segments, yellow-brown, with a thick mucous sheath; on Arrhenatherum elatius, Bromus, Briza media, Calamagrostis villosa, Carex parviflora, Elymus, Elytrigia, Festuca sp., Luzula silvatica, Poa alpina, Poa trivialis,Roegneria, Sesleria coerulea; Triticum aestivum; phen.: V-VIII $ P. trichostoma (Fr.) Fuckel, Symb. Myc.: 215 (1870)
6,7 $ .Sp. 35-50x15-30 µm, with mucous sheath, collapsing very soon; on Luzula lutea, Luzula spadicea; phen.: VII-VIII ..P. ephemera Crivelli, Diss. ETH Zürich 7318: 118 (1983)
7,0 $ Sp. with (6) travisepta $ P. polytricha (Wallr.) Wehm., Pleospora Monograph: 282 (1961)
7,0 $ Sp. cylindrical, 75-105x27-40 µm, with 6-7 travisepta, all segments with longisepta, grey-green, with mucous sheath; graminicolous (Anthoxanthum, Holcus); phen.: VI-VIII $ P. phaeocomes (Rebent.) Fr., Summa Veg. Scand., Section Post.: 397 (1849)
